      "writtenOn": "2022-06-17T16:05:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s possible for the port partner to incorrectly send an ADO_POWER_BUTTON_RELEASE before the ADO_POWER_BUTTON_PRESS or any combination of the two messages.\n\nI think this should be converted into a state machine where you have:\n\nIdle Alert State --\u003e Press Alert State --\u003e Release Alert State\n\n1) Transition from IDLE_STATE to PRESS_STATE on ADO_POWER_BUTTON_PRESS reception\n2) Transition from PRESS_STATE to IDLE_STATE on a timeout (ADO_POWER_BUTTON_RELEASE never received)\n3) Transition from PRESS_STATE to RELEASE_STATE on ADO_POWER_BUTTON_RELEASE reception\n\nPerform the short and long press times in RELEASE_STATE and return to IDLE_STATE",
      "revId": "dfadf696ff086a5ff01687bba7b633d724471439",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ce0f279b_0fa32efd",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
