      "writtenOn": "2022-06-21T21:30:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for your feedback, a state machine sounds good to me. In this patchset, I have moved handling this to a state machine in usb_pd_dpm.c. The PE just needs to check if alerts are a button press or release when it receives them, and call either dpm_handle_pd_button_press(port) or dpm_handle_pd_button_release(port). The state machine in usb_pd_dpm is responsible for tracking presses and releases to decide if any action needs to be taken on the alert.\n\nA couple difference between the state machine you\u0027re describing and what I\u0027ve implemented. There is also a PRESS_STATE -\u003e PRESS_STATE path which resets the timer in a case where the partner sends two consecutive presses. And, given this CL will only handle waking a device from S5/G3 using the USB PD power button, The SM in this CL does not distinguish between short and long presses. Both short and long presses should wake the device from G3/S5. The timeout in PRESS_STATE will still prevent powering on a device when presses exceed the long press time limit.",
      "parentUuid": "ce0f279b_0fa32efd",
      "revId": "dfadf696ff086a5ff01687bba7b633d724471439",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
